      <description>Shenzhen Longsys Electronics Co.’s shares fell in Hong Kong on Tuesday after the company raised HK$7.08 billion ($903 million) in an upsized share sale that’s testing the resilience of investor enthusiasm after a flurry of artificial intelligence supply chain offerings in the city.</description>
